{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>You shall not do injustice in judgment.</b> This warning is directed at litigants, that they not scheme to win according to the law, when it is injustice. Therefore it speaks in the plural: ״לֹא תַעֲשׂוּ״ etc. And the reading of <b>עָוֶל בַּמִּשְׁפָּט</b> is as follows: in the judgment that the judges judge, they should not contrive things so that injustice is present in it. For the judge judges on the basis of the claims that they arrange before him, and therefore Scripture juxtaposes this commandment to the warning of ״לִפְנֵי עִוֵּר״ etc., for this causes the judge to stumble into rendering an unjust judgment." "<b>Further,</b> it intends to say that even if the judgment acquits him, he should not rely on this to commit injustice when he recognizes in himself that injustice is at his right hand. Therefore it speaks in the plural, for it is addressing the litigants, and in what follows — since his intent is to command the judge — it speaks in the singular: ״לֹא תִשָּׂא״, ״לֹא תֶהְדַּר״, and so on." "<b>Further,</b> he intends in saying <b>לֹא תַעֲשׂוּ עָוֶל</b> a warning to the judge: that even if the judgment indicates liability for this one and acquittal for that one, if in his eyes it appears to be injustice — they should not commit this injustice on account of what the law has obligated; rather, the judge has only what his eyes see." "<b>Further,</b> it intends in saying <b>בַּמִּשְׁפָּט</b> with the definite article, after the manner of their saying, of blessed memory (Beitzah 16a), that on Rosh HaShanah the Holy One, blessed be He, apportions to each and every man what he needs according to the judgment of justice. Therefore, if they declare the innocent one liable and acquit the liable one — behold, he produces injustice in the supernal judgment to a set amount. And when they diminish it accordingly, the injustice in the judgment is brought about in that this one did not take what he owes in the heavenly court, and likewise the reverse."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:59:05.876468030Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}